 What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349910 1113 #uuid "e6b6480b-803b-5709-bfd6-a415f8a61bdc" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349910 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=y-2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2 & =4-\\sqrt{z+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2-\\sqrt{z+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=2-\\sqrt{z+3}.$" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349912 13194139535452 true] [17592186349911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349913 13194139535452 true] [17592186349911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349914 13194139535452 true] [17592186349911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349915 13194139535452 true] [17592186349911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349916 13194139535452 true] [17592186349911 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535452 true] [17592186349911 1041 "selection" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349911 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349913 13194139535452 true] [17592186349911 1110 #uuid "b4b9d4a7-e860-5cec-a984-a2c70d4a14ad" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349912 1034 "\\sqrt{z-3}-4" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349912 1111 #uuid "92df6243-48f8-5cdb-b63a-6359bb49b564" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349913 1034 "2-\\sqrt{z+3}" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349913 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349913 1111 #uuid "c80d6a63-78c9-52f1-8d57-1a6e60938d6f" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349914 1034 "\\sqrt{z+3}-2" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349914 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349914 1111 #uuid "ab3e7180-8ff0-5054-8623-c32b5b96de46" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349915 1034 "-\\sqrt{z+3}" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349915 1111 #uuid "89c8be47-aecf-5fc0-9011-c49113af6f21" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349916 1034 "2-\\sqrt{z-3}" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349916 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349916 1111 #uuid "bd7e5249-f949-5cb0-9a10-f15eb7eda5c7" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349917 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349918 13194139535452 true] [17592186349917 1089 "q-108840" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349917 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535452 true] [17592186349917 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x+y+2)^{3}-1.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=C-2x,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349917 1113 #uuid "a5960cef-60ff-556a-97c3-b6b4d81204a8" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349917 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =(z+2)^{3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=(z+2)^{3}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(z+2)^{3}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{(z+2)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2(z+2)^{2}} & =x+K \\\\ \\frac{1}{(z+2)^{2}} & =C-2x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-2K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{(x+y+2)^{2}}=C-2x\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)=\\frac{1}{(x+y+2)^{2}}.$" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349918 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349919 13194139535452 true] [17592186349918 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349920 13194139535452 true] [17592186349918 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349921 13194139535452 true] [17592186349918 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349922 13194139535452 true] [17592186349918 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349923 13194139535452 true] [17592186349918 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535452 true] [17592186349918 1041 "selection" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349918 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349920 13194139535452 true] [17592186349918 1110 #uuid "5b05e9b8-e0c7-5607-aff6-3b8f3ac74bef" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349919 1034 "\\frac{(x+y+2)^{3}}{3}" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349919 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349919 1111 #uuid "86939afe-56b6-53f3-a0d5-2d52e6b24cb0" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349920 1034 "\\frac{1}{(x+y+2)^{2}}" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349920 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349920 1111 #uuid "3d6b97fc-2ea3-59ef-baed-9571f2781497" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349921 1034 "-\\frac{2}{(x+y+2)^{2}}" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349921 1111 #uuid "b24bbd98-668a-502f-812d-e9af3017b6ab" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349922 1034 "-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{4}}" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349922 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349922 1111 #uuid "cfda16f7-23cf-5f60-a16b-b1f024a1afbe" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349923 1034 "\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349923 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349923 1111 #uuid "2a88c86c-e675-5079-9414-2c99efda24f7" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349924 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349925 13194139535452 true] [17592186349924 1089 "q-108841" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349924 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535452 true] [17592186349924 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{x+y}-x-y}{x+y}.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=C-x,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349924 1113 #uuid "ae9cc299-d899-5b37-90ea-45ac33d8f95e" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349924 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\frac{{e}^{z}-z}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{z}}{z}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{z}{{e}^{z}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int z{e}^{-z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing integration by parts on the left side,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=z & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-z} & \\,⟹\\,v=-{e}^{-z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int z{e}^{-z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -z{e}^{-z}+\\int {e}^{-z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -z{e}^{-z}-{e}^{-z} & =x+C \\\\ -{e}^{-z}(z+1) & =x+K \\\\ {e}^{-z}(z+1) & =C-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n{e}^{-x-y}(x+y+1)=C-x\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)={e}^{-x-y}(x+y+1).$" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349925 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349926 13194139535452 true] [17592186349925 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349927 13194139535452 true] [17592186349925 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349928 13194139535452 true] [17592186349925 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349929 13194139535452 true] [17592186349925 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349930 13194139535452 true] [17592186349925 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535452 true] [17592186349925 1041 "selection" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349925 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349928 13194139535452 true] [17592186349925 1110 #uuid "55b22758-4dde-5137-a81c-ee58cc7f76fa" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349926 1034 "{e}^{x+y}(x+y)" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349926 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349926 1111 #uuid "4de35554-39cc-52a6-a103-7b8fadab01e9" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349927 1034 "{e}^{-x-y}" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349927 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349927 1111 #uuid "cf7372b5-6acf-59c9-8ef1-a23dead09b7c" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349928 1034 "{e}^{-x-y}(x+y+1)" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349928 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349928 1111 #uuid "2b92939f-8e01-5592-9b8e-09846d94262d" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349929 1034 "{e}^{x+y}(1-x-y)" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349929 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349929 1111 #uuid "4c0286ca-74ce-56e7-ba06-b9748eaad082" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349930 1034 "{e}^{-2x-2y}" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349930 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535452 true] [17592186349930 1111 #uuid "067018ac-0e05-5cd8-9466-485e165735af" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349931 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349932 13194139535452 true] [17592186349931 1089 "q-149710" 13194139535452 true] [17592186349931 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535452 true] [17592186349931 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt[3]{x-2y}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x-2y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535